{{Navbar modding}}
<translate>
'''Modpacks''' or the act of '''modpacking''' involves taking multiple mods and combining them into a single mod that is then distributed as a unified [[Steam Workshop]] item. The objective is to provide users, and more importantly servers, with stable mod versions as any update to mods used on servers require the server to restart to update said mods to allow users with the updated versions to join the server.

This pratice is by default both not allowed and discouraged by the official modding policy. This pratice is harmful to the original mods as this is often done wrongly, which leads to the mod's packed [[Load order|clashing]] with the original mods, and leads to confusing and nonsensical bug reports to the original mod creators (as their mod is flagged as the culprit) when the problem doesn't come from their version of the mod. A feature was planned for [[Build 42]] to load mods associated to their [[Workshop ID]] but this has been scrapped as there are concerns to this solution making mod development annoying to manage if not outright pure hell.

For more information about the official policies that limit this pratice, see the [[Modding#Terms & Conditions|Terms & Conditions]] of modding.

== Navigation ==
</translate>

